/*! @brief A plain-object dictionary of event listeners, keyed by event name

 EventMap is the typed form of the listener maps accepted by
 `EventEmitter#on/addListener/prependListener/once/prependOnceListener/off`
 and `removeListener`, and by the map forms of the Redis subscription methods
 (`Redis#sub/unsub/psub/unpsub`). It is a regular JavaScript object dictionary
 (not an ES `Map`); the property names are event or channel names.

 Every value must be a function. The map is processed in property order, and a
 value that is not a function fails with an invalid-type error while entries
 already processed stay registered. EventMap is input-only: read listeners
 back with `listeners()`, `rawListeners()` or `listenerCount()`.

 Example 1 — register several listeners at once:
 ```JavaScript
 const EventEmitter = require('events');

 const emitter = new EventEmitter();
 emitter.on({
     connect: () => { },
     close: () => { }
 });
 console.log(emitter.listenerCount('connect')); // 1
 ```

 Example 2 — one-shot listeners:
 ```JavaScript
 const EventEmitter = require('events');

 const emitter = new EventEmitter();
 emitter.once({ ready: () => { } });
 console.log(emitter.listenerCount('ready')); // 1
 ```
*/
map EventMap: Function(...args) => Value;
